      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you know why it doesn\u0027t print \u0027boot_mode: 0x01 -\u003e 0x00\u0027? IIUC, Cr50 reads boot_mode from scratchpad. So, on wake-up from deep sleep, boot_mode should be still 0x01.\n\nHere is what I see on my Redrix when esc+power+refresh are pressed with Cr50 in deep sleep:\n\n--- UART initialized after reboot ---\n[Reset cause: hibernate rbox]\n[Image: RW_B, 0.6.92/cr50_v2.0.3394-8b4a861205 ...]\n[0.003673 Inits done]\n[0.005088 power button pressed]\n[0.005996 init_jittery_clock_locking_optional: run level high, request to enable]\n[0.038539 init took 25550]\n[0.042419 update_rollback_mask: bailing out at bit 1]\n[0.044258 update_rollback_mask: bailing out at bit 3]\n[0.046951 combo0 efs rst]\n\nI also don\u0027t see\u00270x01 -\u003e 0x00\u0027. Maybe ec_efs_init_ is called after this?",
